cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PAVO-Bench or the meta-controller in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PAVO: Pipeline-Aware Voice Orchestration with Demand-Conditioned Inference Routing"
abstract: >
  PAVO treats the ASR-LLM-TTS voice pipeline as a jointly optimizable inference graph
  with demand-conditioned routing. An 85,041-parameter meta-controller is trained
  with multi-objective PPO in 106 seconds on H100. A committed 200-sample mixed
  measured/simulated summary reports a 10.3% P95 end-to-end latency reduction;
  its adaptive row is heuristic aggregate sampling rather than checkpoint replay.
  In five catalog-simulation replications, the paired
  mean-latency test gives p = 2x10^-6. The manuscript reports a 71% per-turn energy
  reduction vs a fixed-cloud baseline on a 50,000-turn simulated benchmark; the
  standalone routing trace is not included. Hard-constraint masking on the
  inter-stage coupling study includes a 5,400-call H100 aggregate across three
  LLM families and a preliminary 30-question Apple M3 pilot. The manuscript
  reports that hard-constraint masking reduces coherence-failure rate from 7.1%
  to 0.9% (7.9x), at +110 ms median latency cost.
